// Ch4 C4-02 "Haluna, wake night", bark 1 of 3: the lane. The child from Ch3's night bark ("Teach me
// tomorrow") teaches Rhen the end of the skipping rhyme, as promised. The same rhyme as Ch2's lane
// bark; tonight Rhen almost hears it. Field bark, no camera cues. Written warm, never as a clue.
title: ch04_bark_lane_rhyme
location: ch04/haluna_wake
---
Child [smile]: You said teach you. So listen. ...three for the bell and four for the hush, and then you start again. #line:ch04_bark_rhyme_001
Rhen [neutral]: Start what again? #line:ch04_bark_rhyme_002
Child [laugh]: The rhyme. Everybody knows that. #line:ch04_bark_rhyme_003
